report:
Audit-only Phase 1, src/slack.rs + src/telegram.rs + src/discord.rs fully read (raw, all lines).

[Medium] Telegram offset confirms updates before they are durably handled. src/telegram.rs:148-166.
```rust
if let Some(id) = u["update_id"].as_i64() {
    self.offset.fetch_max(id + 1, Ordering::Relaxed); // L157 confirmed to Telegram
}
...
self.pending.lock().await.extend(it); // L165 in-memory only
```
Scenario: batch of 3 messages arrives; offset is confirmed to id+1 regardless of processing; the agent turn for message 1 runs, then the process crashes/redeploys; the pending VecDeque dies. On restart getUpdates resumes from the confirmed offset, so Telegram never redelivers messages 2-3 — permanent message loss. Fix: confirm each offset only after the bridge consumes the message, or persist pending.

[Medium] Discord op 7/op 9 reconnect on fixed 5s sleep can exhaust the ~1000/day identify quota (5s cadence is ~17000/day) and get the bot gateway-banned for up to 24h. src/discord.rs:329-334, also 294-295.
```rust
if v["op"] == 7 || v["op"] == 9 {
    *guard = None;
    drop(guard);
    tokio::time::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_secs(5)).await;
    continue;
}
```
Scenario: persistent op 9 invalid-session (outage, flagged account) makes recv re-identify every ~5s, tripping the account-level identify ban. The code comment acknowledges this exact risk but 5s is insufficient; op 9 needs long/exponential backoff distinct from op 7.

[Low] Slack seen_envelopes clears the entire set at the 4096 cap, so a late retry of a recent envelope is reprocessed (duplicate agent turn, duplicate permission prompt). src/slack.rs:270-277.
```rust
if seen.len() >= 4096 {
    seen.clear();
}
if !seen.insert(eid.to_string()) {
    continue;
}
```
Scenario: busy channel, Slack retries envelope E after 4096 newer envelopes were processed; the clear erased E, so it runs twice. Evicting only the oldest entry keeps the bound without this loss.

CLEAN (dedup material for next audits): token-in-URL sanitized on every reqwest error path in telegram.rs (44-51, 86-93, and all map_err(sanitize) call sites including the 429-retry branch); slack/discord tokens via bearer header/WS payload only; 429/Retry-After honored in all three senders (f64 parse, 30s cap, 1.0 default, single-retry contract consistent); timeouts present everywhere (connect 10s / total 30s; getUpdates per-request timeout_secs+10; WS liveness 60s slack / 2x heartbeat+15s discord — no hang path); only intentional `let _ =` is the Slack ack (Slack retry + dedup absorb it); UTF-8-safe splitting via floor_char_boundary in all three senders (stable since Rust 1.87 — cargo check --lib passed, exit 0, unstable-API suspicion disproven); parsers reject empty post-strip text, skip bot/self authors, discord handles the <@!id> nickname variant, telegram blocks bot authors (prevents third-party bot self-approval); discord hello validated, heartbeat_interval clamped above 0, heartbeat task aborted on Drop (no leak); slack acks every envelope including skipped ones.

NOT AUDITED: channel.rs Bridge loop error policy (affects finding 1's loss window; ChannelCore scope); exact Slack idle-ping cadence vs the 60s threshold (docs confirm pings exist, exact period unverified).
